<NAME>Principal actuary: 5 years.</NAME>
<CONTENT>In the Police Retirement System of St. Louis (PRS-STL) actuarial RFP, the principal actuary assigned to provide services to PRS-STL must have a minimum of five (5) years of professional actuarial experience.

The relevant language appears in Section IV.D, “Mandatory Minimum Qualifications,” item 3, which says the principal actuary must:
- have a minimum of five (5) years professional actuarial experience,
- be an enrolled actuary,
- be a Member of the American Academy of Actuaries, and
- be an Associate of the Society of Actuaries, although Fellowship is preferred.

The RFP also separately requires, in item 4 of the same section, that the principal actuary have a minimum of five (5) years of experience testifying before legislative and administrative bodies in support of actuarial positions and/or valuation principles.</CONTENT>
