# Markdown Briefing

## Answer
The **principal actuary must have a minimum of five (5) years of professional actuarial experience**.

## Supporting Context
According to the PRS-STL actuarial RFP, in **Section IV.D, “Mandatory Minimum Qualifications,” item 3**, the principal actuary must:

- have at least **five (5) years** of professional actuarial experience,
- be an **enrolled actuary**,
- be a **Member of the American Academy of Actuaries**, and
- be an **Associate of the Society of Actuaries** (with Fellowship preferred).

## Additional Note
The RFP also separately requires **five (5) years of experience testifying** before legislative and administrative bodies in support of actuarial positions and/or valuation principles.
